# Line endings: LF in the repository, LF in the working tree, on every machine.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true on Windows rewrote the entire working tree to CRLF on
# each checkout while the repository itself kept LF. Harmless to git, and quietly
# confusing to everything else: a scripted edit matching on "\n" stops matching after a
# checkout, and every commit prints a "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning per file.
#
# Content-neutral to add — every text file in the index was already LF when this landed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so line endings are never touched and diffs are never attempted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.apk binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
